spot with g_Ca = 0 and frozen-K+ (strictly linear RC) ablations, an inter-input delay sweep dt in [0, 30] ms, and the resulting coincidence window dt_c (5.24 ms at bf = 0.20 -> 0.73 ms at bf = 1), supralinear gain (4.28x vs exact linear 2.000000), same-branch fraction (1.00 -> 0.00) and Pearson r(window, bf) = -0.698 (p = 0.054); transfer_boundary: 2D planar fan and 3D cubic Euclidean carrier-point greedy MST arbors with Rall 3/2 passive electrotonic diameter tapering mapped to Cajal's Golgi-stained Purkinje neuron drawing; the specimen reference values in `cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json` (D_f = 1.7817, Sholl peak = 73, hubs = 62) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs recorded as regression anchors, not independent literature morphometrics | (Pass 3) The dendritic Ca2+ hotspot is a single isopotential Morris-Lecar compartment with the canonical barnacle Hopf parameter set (C = 20 uF/cm2, Rinzel & Ermentrout 1998), not a Purkinje P-type Ca2+ channel fit; passive attenuation to the hotspot uses the semi-infinite-cylinder factor exp(-X), exact for Rall-matched equivalent cylinders viewed from the soma and approximate centripetally; the synaptic peak current I_peak = 110 uA/cm2 is a protocol choice tuned so single inputs stay sub-threshold | (Pass 3) Roth & Häusser (2001) passive constants and all five new DOIs were transcribed offline and are flagged as not re-verified in `electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json`, the dataset README and the BibTeX file; does_not_claim: Purkinje P-type Ca2+ channel kinetics fitted to Llinás & Sugimori (1980) recordings, a multi-compartment active cable (NEURON-style) hotspot, Na+ dendritic spikes, activity-dependent filopodial synaptotropic retraction, or an empirical coincidence-window value from the literature (the 3 ms reference is tau_syn and the -1 reference is the predicted sign)]; other sources: Biophysics of Computation: Information Processing in Single Neurons <https://global.oup.com/academic/product/biophysics-of-computation