<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Code-to-model traceability: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-73) maps every governing equation — greedy cost, 2D/3D scaling, Rall 3/2, lambda_DC and the Koch AC reduction, the Morris-Lecar ODEs — to its paper and to the five Lean 4 theorems by name, and each Pass 3 function carries a docstring naming the equation it implements and the ablation it exposes (L352-368, L425-461). The math-KG YAML registers equations 1-5 with single-range `code_locus` pins re-pointed to the shifted lines, and every measurement `source` names the theorem it leans on. Deductions: the JSON `linear_superposition_note` (L62) attributes exact superposition to \"Lean 4 Theorem 5\" whereas the script and the Lean file number it Theorem 4 (`rall_passive_membrane_linear_superposition`) and Theorem 5 is the length-constant bound (-2); the docstring Lean line pins for Theorems 1-3 (L36-67, L85-113, L127-147) are approximate against the 216-line module (theorem heads at L38, L90, L136) and Theorems 4-5 carry no line pin (-2); `evaluate_cuntz_pareto_sweep` cites no figure for the benchmark arrays it compares against (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
