<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Cuntz (2007, 2010) greedy MST solver with bottom-up Rall (1959) 3/2 diameter accumulation (`grow_cuntz_dendritic_tree`, L165-281), the random spanning-tree ablation (L282-313), the 8-point bf Pareto sweep (L716-769) and the 2D/3D Wen-Chklovskii scaling regressions (L770-828) are unchanged from v2 and remain faithful. Pass 3 adds a genuinely coupled passive/active model: the Rall DC length constant and Koch (1999) Eq. 2.37 AC reduction (`rall_length_constant_um`, L352-368) are the textbook formulas, every edge receives X_e = l_e / lambda_f(d_e) from the Rall diameters (`compute_tree_electrotonics`, L371-388), and the Morris-Lecar equations (L425-461) are correctly transcribed with the two ablation switches that isolate the regenerative g_Ca term. Deductions: the hotspot is a single isopotential compartment with the canonical barnacle Hopf parameter set (C = 20 uF/cm2, V1-V4, phi) rather than Purkinje P-type Ca2+ kinetics, so the 4.28x gain and the 5.24 ms window are properties of a generic excitable membrane placed at the LCA, not of a Purkinje dendrite (-3); attenuation uses the semi-infinite exp(-X) factor (L483-484), which is only exact for Rall-matched cylinders seen from the soma, whereas here it is applied centripetally from tips toward a branch node (-2); the scaling-law sweep runs at bf = 0.15 (L791, L801) while every other panel uses the Purkinje regime bf = 0.20 (-1). Five Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) back the greedy cost trade-off, the 3/2 law, tree topology, exact passive superposition and lambda_f <= lambda_DC." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L425–L461: Vectorised forward-Euler Morris-Lecar Ca2+/K+ hotspot with g_ca_scale = 0 and freeze_w ablations; parameters are the canonical barnacle Hopf set, not a Purkinje P-type fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L425-L461>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Morphometric validation: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1163-1342) now returns 15 reference-anchored measurements: the 9 v2 metrics (Pareto W/W0 r = 1.0000, P/P1 r = 0.99969, bf = 0.20 W/W0 = 1.0189 vs 1.0220 with a 10.43x random ablation, alpha_2D = 0.4797 +- 0.0168, alpha_3D = 0.6495 +- 0.0456, Rall ratio 1.0000, D_f, Sholl peak, hubs) plus 6 Pass 3 metrics with explicit nulls and ablations: lambda_f / lambda_DC = 0.2487 against a hand-computed analytic check, passive superposition ratio 1.000000 against the Lean-proved null, active gain 4.28x against the linear 2.0 with the g_Ca = 0 ablation (2.05x) reported alongside, window 5.24 ms, same-branch fraction 0.0 in the star limit, and r(window, bf) = -0.698. Each `source`/`note` says honestly whether the reference is empirical, analytic or a model prediction. Deductions: three of the nine v2 references (D_f = 1.7817, 73, 62) are the script's own outputs (L1256, L1266, L1276), so those three \"matches\" are tautological (-3); of the six new metrics only the analytic ratio and the two exact nulls have a defensible reference — the window reference (3 ms = tau_syn) and the sign reference (-1) are model predictions and the gain reference is the linear null, so no Pass 3 number is compared with a measured dendritic spike or summation curve (-3); the coincidence window is defined as the largest grid offset still firing (L523-527), which quantises it to the 2.5 ms grid and assigns 0.0 to a pair that fires only at dt = 0 (indistinguishable from a non-firing pair) (-1); Pearson r over 8 bf points has p = 0.054 and is reported as a sign test (-1); I_peak = 110 uA/cm2 is tuned so singles never fire and pairs fire at bf = 0.20 (JSON L51), which makes the single-input fraction 0 an outcome of the protocol (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L1251–L1280: Specimen D_f / Sholl peak / hubs measurements whose reference_value (1.7817, 73, 62) equals the script's own output by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L1251-L1280>",
        "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L1312–L1341: Window and Pearson-sign measurements whose reference_value is tau_syn = 3 ms and the predicted sign -1 (model predictions, labelled as such in source/note) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L1312-L1341>",
        "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L523–L527: Coincidence window = largest swept offset still firing; a pair firing only at dt = 0 gets 0.0 and the 2.5 ms grid quantises the result <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L523-L527>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-2d-planar-dendritic-wiring-scaling-exponent-alpha-2d-w-propto-n-alpha-2d>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-3d-volumetric-dendritic-wiring-scaling-exponent-alpha-3d-w-propto-n-alpha-3d>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-active-morris-lecar-ca2-hotspot-supralinear-paired-single-peak-gain-at-bf-0-20>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-cajal-1899-purkinje-specimen-box-counting-fractal-dimension-d-f>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-cajal-1899-purkinje-specimen-peak-sholl-intersection-count>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-cajal-1899-purkinje-specimen-skeletonized-primary-secondary-bifurcation-hubs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-coincidence-window-vs-cuntz-balancing-factor-pearson-correlation-across-bf-in-0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-cuntz-balancing-factor-sweep-normalized-conduction-path-p-bf-p-1-correlation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-cuntz-balancing-factor-sweep-normalized-wiring-cost-w-bf-w-0-correlation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-dendritic-ca2-spike-coincidence-window-delta-t-c-at-bf-0-20-purkinje-regime>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-passive-linear-rc-g-ca-0-k-gate-frozen-hotspot-superposition-ratio-v-pair-v-a-v-b>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-purkinje-class-iv-regime-bf-0-20-normalized-wiring-cost-w-w-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-rall-passive-cable-ac-dc-length-constant-ratio-lambda-f-lambda-dc-at-the-synaptic-frequency>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-rall-s-3-2-electrotonic-impedance-matching-ratio-sum-d-daughter-3-2-d-parent-3-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-measurement-same-branch-shared-lca-hotspot-fraction-of-nearest-neighbour-tip-pairs-in-the-bf-1-radial-star-limit>,
