        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — MorphoEval overall 92.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py` (overall weighted score 92.2/100, down from 93.8/100 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed: Section 2b (L315-L712) couples Rall/Koch passive-cable electrotonics on every Rall-3/2 edge of every Cuntz tree to an active Morris-Lecar Ca2+ hotspot at the lowest common ancestor of nearest-neighbour terminal-tip pairs, and evaluates synaptic coincidence detection across all 8 Cuntz balancing factors (window 5.24 ms at bf = 0.20 -> 0.73 ms at bf = 1; supralinear gain 4.28x vs the exactly-linear null 2.000000 of the frozen-K+ ablation; same-branch fraction 1.00 -> 0.00; r(window, bf) = -0.698). The exact linear superposition null and the lambda_f <= lambda_DC bound are machine-checked in Lean 4 (Theorems 4-5, 0 sorrys), the new reference table is SHA-256-pinned, 6 new measurements bring the total to 15 and the self-test to 10 suites. The score nevertheless falls because the audit of the new layer exposed deeper defects the v2 audit did not penalise: the Cajal specimen \"reference\" values are the script's own outputs (match by construction), the Cuntz Pareto benchmark arrays carry no digitisation provenance, the five Pass 3 sources and the Purkinje passive constants were transcribed offline and not re-verified, the hotspot is a canonical barnacle Morris-Lecar compartment rather than a Purkinje P-type fit, and the coincidence-window metric is quantised to a 2.5 ms grid with a Pearson r over 8 points that does not reach significance (p = 0.054). Overall 92.2/100 (faithfulness 91.8, reproducibility 93.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 95, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/cajal_dendritic_wiring_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py at 45670cb8, image/png, 1031857 B, 2475×1560 px, artifact_sha256 d8a5eea145746b4df580c95c55b83255c17ede5c82986441d0dadf63208aca34 (sha256 d8a5eea145746b4df580c95c55b83255c17ede5c82986441d0dadf63208aca34), spec_fingerprint a6977d117c117453a3da70243bb87c40c9868192a748b42afa7ab4730c025791. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a6977d117c117453a3da70243bb87c40c9868192a748b42afa7ab4730c025791; artifact_sha256: d8a5eea145746b4df580c95c55b83255c17ede5c82986441d0dadf63208aca34; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json=e437ed8419f90b10..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_purkinje_dendritic_arbor_specimen.jpg=6255a396655b56c4..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json=adf04c13baa46a5e..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/paper_citations.bib=c8a87e40791184dc..., datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/scout_manifest.json=2440e61b14fedf53...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-cajal-dendritic-wiring-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cuntz, Forstner, Borst & Häusser (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. 6(8):e1000877 & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS 104:13319-13324 greedy Minimum Spanning Tree dendritic growth rule minimizing C(u, v) = ||u - v|| + bf * path(u, root) across balancing factor bf in [0, 1] to balance Ramón y Cajal's (1899) conservation of cytoplasmic wiring length W and conduction time P | Wen & Chklovskii (2008) J. Neurophysiol. 99:2320-2328 & Cuntz et al. (2010) dimensional wiring scaling laws W propto N^(1/2) A^(1/2) in 2D planar arbors and W propto N^(2/3) V^(1/3) in 3D volumetric arbors | Rall (1959) Exp. Neurol. 1:491-527 electrotonic input-conductance impedance-matching power law d_parent^(3/2) = sum_k d_daughter_k^(3/2) and the passive cable length constant lambda_DC = sqrt(R_m d / 4 R_i); Koch (1999) Eq. 2.37 sinusoidal steady-state reduction lambda_f = lambda_DC sqrt(2 / (1 + sqrt(1 + (omega tau_m)^2))) | Roth & Häusser (2001) J. Physiol. 535:445-472 Purkinje passive constants (R_m ~ 122 kOhm cm2, R_i ~ 115 Ohm cm, C_m ~ 0.77 uF/cm2); Llinás & Sugimori (1980) J. Physiol. 305:197-213 all-or-none Purkinje dendritic Ca2+ spikes; Polsky, Mel & Schiller (2004) Nat. Neurosci. 7:621-627 within-branch supralinear vs between-branch linear synaptic summation; Morris & Lecar (1981) Biophys. J. 35:193-213 two-variable Ca2+/K+ membrane; reconstructed_in_script: Full Cuntz et al. (2010) greedy MST solver (`grow_cuntz_dendritic_tree`) across 8 balancing factors bf in [0.0, 1.0] on N = 160 synaptic carriers, reproducing normalized wiring cost W(bf)/W(0) (Pearson r = 1.0000, RMSE = 0.0042) and normalized conduction path P(bf)/P(1) (Pearson r = 0.99969, RMSE = 0.0067), plus a random spanning tree negative control (10.43x wiring inflation) | Log-log OLS scaling law verification across N in [25, 320] at bf = 0.15: alpha_2D = 0.4797 +- 0.0168 (vs 0.5000), alpha_3D = 0.6495 +- 0.0456 (vs 0.6667), bf = 1.0 star limit alpha_star = 0.9996 | Bottom-up Rall 3/2 electrotonic diameter assignment verifying (sum d_daughter^(3/2))/d_parent^(3/2) = 1.0000 (RMSE = 1.27e-16 across 40 bifurcations) | Computer-vision segmentation of Santiago Ramón y Cajal's (1899) human cerebellar Purkinje neuron drawing (`cajal_purkinje_dendritic_arbor_specimen.jpg`, Museo Cajal 328 Madrid): box-counting fractal dimension D_f = 1.7817 +- 0.0248, peak Sholl intersection count = 73 at r/R_max = 0.6176, 62 primary/secondary bifurcation hubs | (Pass 3) Rall/Koch passive-cable electrotonics on every Rall-3/2 edge of every Cuntz tree (X_e = l_e / lambda_f(d_e), lambda_f / lambda_DC = 0.2487 at f_syn = 53.05 Hz), exp(-X) attenuation of two alpha-synapse inputs from the 24 nearest-neighbour terminal-tip pairs to their lowest-common-ancestor hotspot, a vectorised forward-Euler Morris-Lecar Ca2+/K+ hotspot with g_Ca = 0 and frozen-K+ (strictly linear RC) ablations, an inter-input delay sweep dt in [0, 30] ms, and the resulting coincidence window dt_c (5.24 ms at bf = 0.20 -> 0.73 ms at bf = 1), supralinear gain (4.28x vs exact linear 2.000000), same-branch fraction (1.00 -> 0.00) and Pearson r(window, bf) = -0.698 (p = 0.054); transfer_boundary: 2D planar fan and 3D cubic Euclidean carrier-point greedy MST arbors with Rall 3/2 passive electrotonic diameter tapering mapped to Cajal's Golgi-stained Purkinje neuron drawing; the specimen reference values in `cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json` (D_f = 1.7817, Sholl peak = 73, hubs = 62) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs recorded as regression anchors, not independent literature morphometrics | (Pass 3) The dendritic Ca2+ hotspot is a single isopotential Morris-Lecar compartment with the canonical barnacle Hopf parameter set (C = 20 uF/cm2, Rinzel & Ermentrout 1998), not a Purkinje P-type Ca2+ channel fit; passive attenuation to the hotspot uses the semi-infinite-cylinder factor exp(-X), exact for Rall-matched equivalent cylinders viewed from the soma and approximate centripetally; the synaptic peak current I_peak = 110 uA/cm2 is a protocol choice tuned so single inputs stay sub-threshold | (Pass 3) Roth & Häusser (2001) passive constants and all five new DOIs were transcribed offline and are flagged as not re-verified in `electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json`, the dataset README and the BibTeX file; does_not_claim: Purkinje P-type Ca2+ channel kinetics fitted to Llinás & Sugimori (1980) recordings, a multi-compartment active cable (NEURON-style) hotspot, Na+ dendritic spikes, activity-dependent filopodial synaptotropic retraction, or an empirical coincidence-window value from the literature (the 3 ms reference is tau_syn and the -1 reference is the predicted sign)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:1163-1174, 1141 and 615-616 — `measure_morphoeval()` ignores the CLI parameters and the Pareto star marker / coincidence figure hard-code bf = 0.20 (index 2), so `--bf`, `--n-carriers`, `--radius`, `--seed` overrides are not reflected in the measurements or in those panels. Thread the CLI namespace through `measure_morphoeval(n_carriers, radius, seed, bf)` and the figure helpers.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:403-422 — `nearest_neighbour_tip_pairs()` requests 24 pairs but the bf = 0 / 0.2 trees have fewer than 48 leaves (19 / 21 pairs used), so per-bf means are over different pair sets. Fix the pair count to min over bf (or report n_pairs per bf in the figure and the measurement `method`).",
        "remediation needed: 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:425-461 and datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json:29-47 — the Ca2+ hotspot is a single isopotential Morris-Lecar compartment with the canonical barnacle Hopf set (C = 20 uF/cm2), so the 4.28x gain and 5.24 ms window are generic excitable-membrane properties. Fit g_Ca / g_K kinetics and C_m to Llinás & Sugimori (1980) Purkinje P-type dendritic Ca2+ spikes (amplitude, width, threshold) and resolve the hotspot as a multi-compartment active cable (NEURON-style) instead of the semi-infinite exp(-X) attenuation at L483-484.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:523-527 and 579-604 — the coincidence window is the largest 2.5 ms grid offset still firing (a pair firing only at dt = 0 gets 0.0, same as a non-firing pair), and r(window, bf) uses 8 points (p = 0.054). Interpolate the firing boundary between grid points (or bisect dt per pair), separate \"fires at dt = 0 only\" from \"never fires\", and extend the bf sweep (e.g. 16-21 values) so the sign test reaches significance or is reported as not significant.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json:45-49 and 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:740-749 — the Cuntz Pareto benchmark arrays (W/W0 ending in the 11.50 outlier, P/P1, bifurcation angles) have no figure/panel/digitisation provenance, and the headline r = 1.0000 is dominated by the bf = 1 outlier. Record the source figure, panel, digitisation method and per-point uncertainty; report r on bf in [0, 0.7] excluding the star limit, and report the 4-dp r = 1.0000 as 0.99998.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json:88-102 with 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:1251-1280 and 1386-1390 — the specimen references D_f = 1.7817, Sholl peak = 73, hubs = 62 are the script's own Pass 2 outputs written back into the dataset, so three of the 15 \"matches\" are tautological. Replace them with an independent morphometric (e.g. published Purkinje Sholl peak / fractal dimension from a NeuroMorpho.org reconstruction or a second, independently segmented Cajal drawing) and relabel the current values as regression anchors in the JSON and in `measure_morphoeval()` `source`.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json:6-8 and datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/README.md:32-38 — Roth & Häusser (2001) R_m / R_i / C_m and the five Pass 3 DOIs were transcribed offline and flagged \"NOT re-verified\"; verify them against the papers (Roth & Häusser Table 2 / text values; DOIs via Crossref) and update the JSON note, README, BibTeX and this audit's `references` block.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json:62 and 2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py:53-72 — the JSON note cites \"Lean 4 Theorem 5\" for exact superposition (Theorem 4 in the script and Lean module), and the docstring Lean line pins for Theorems 1-3 (L36-67, L85-113, L127-147) are approximate while Theorems 4-5 have none. Correct the theorem number (requires re-pinning the JSON SHA-256 at L337) and pin all five theorems to the current 216-line module (heads at L38, L90, L136, L170, L200)." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.22e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Parameter expressivity: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Sweeps 8 balancing factors bf in [0.0, 1.0] (L716-769) and N in [25, 320] in 2D, 3D and star regimes (L770-828) as in v2; Pass 3 adds the inter-input delay sweep dt in [0, 30] ms (13 points) and runs the whole coincidence protocol across all 8 bf trees (`evaluate_coincidence_across_bf`, L579-604), so the new mechanism is parameter-controlled by bf and its tuning curves are rendered per bf (figure Panel C). The `--bf` CLI flag, dead in v2, is now honoured for Panel A, Panel E and the GIF (L962-965) together with `--n-carriers`, `--radius` and `--seed` (L1459-1464). Deductions: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1163-1174) takes no arguments and always uses the default N/seed/radius, so the measurements reported after a CLI override describe the default run, not the rendered one (-3); the Pareto-panel star marker (L1141) and the coincidence figure (L615-616) still fix bf = 0.20 / sweep index 2 regardless of `--bf` (-2); none of the Pass 3 physiological parameters (I_peak, tau_syn, g_Ca, R_m) is exposed on the CLI or swept — only bf is (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L1141–L1141: Pareto star marker hard-coded to sweep index 2 (bf = 0.20) regardless of --bf; same for the coincidence figure at L615-616 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L1141-L1141>",
        "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L1163–L1174: measure_morphoeval() ignores CLI parameters: always default carriers/seed/radius <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L1163-L1174>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-parameter-expressivity-1>,
