<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Reproducibility package: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`self_test()` (L1349-1453) now runs 10 deterministic suites in 8.9-11 s: SHA-256 integrity of all three pinned inputs, Betti_1 = 0 topology, Pareto monotonicity/correlation, random-tree control, 2D/3D scaling, Rall 3/2, specimen CV, the 15-metric bitwise-determinism contract (L1392-1396), and the Pass 3 suites 9-10 (L1398-1445: lambda_DC analytic check, lambda_f < lambda_DC, exact superposition < 1e-9, active gain > 2, single-input fraction 0 for every bf, star-limit same-branch 0, window shrinks and tip->hotspot X grows at bf = 1, r(window, bf) < 0). The default render regenerates the PNG, the GIF (byte-identical) and the new coincidence PNG in 7.7 s; the Lean module verifies in 0.3 s with 0 sorrys. Deductions: `docs/media/*.png` are gitignored (`.gitignore` rule `*.png`), so neither the comparison PNG nor the new coincidence PNG is versioned and the reproducibility of the figures the audit judged rests on re-running the script (-3); the README / self-test description in v2 (\"passing in < 1 s\") is no longer accurate — the 10-suite run takes ~9 s because it executes `measure_morphoeval()` twice (-1); there is no lock file pinning the exact numpy/scipy/matplotlib versions used (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-repro-package-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-repro-package-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Source and data traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The six v2 sources keep their verified DOIs in the docstring, README and BibTeX; the reference JSON, the specimen JPEG and the new `electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json` are all SHA-256-pinned and verified fail-closed at runtime (`verify_dataset_integrity` L117-142, `load_electrotonic_reference` L340-349, constants L99-100 and L337). Pass 3 adds five BibTeX entries (bib L66-120) and a README addendum (README L22-38) with the model-reduction and the offline-transcription caveat stated plainly. Deductions: the five new DOIs and the Roth & Häusser (2001) passive constants were transcribed from memory and are flagged \"NOT re-verified online\" (JSON L8; README L32), so the Purkinje R_m / R_i / C_m that set every electrotonic length rest on assertion (-4); the Cuntz Pareto benchmark arrays (`balancing_factor_pareto_benchmarks`, reference JSON L45-49: W/W0 1.0 ... 11.50, P/P1 1.68 ... 1.0, angles) carry no figure/panel/digitisation provenance although the headline Pearson r = 1.0000 is computed against them (L740-749) (-3); the specimen *_ref values are self-generated (see specimen-match) and are not labelled as such in the JSON (-1); Koch (1999) Eq. 2.37 and the Rinzel & Ermentrout (1998) Hopf set are cited without page pinpoints (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json L45–L49: balancing_factor_pareto_benchmarks arrays with no figure/panel/digitisation provenance; W/W0 ref ends in the 11.50 outlier that dominates r = 1.0000 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json#L45-L49>",
        "datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json L6–L8: passive_cable_constants.note: Roth & Häusser (2001) R_m/R_i/C_m transcribed from memory and NOT re-verified online <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json#L6-L8>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The vendored, SHA-256-verified Cajal (1899) Purkinje drawing is segmented as in v2 (`segment_cajal_purkinje_specimen`, L833-934: arbor mask, EDT soma, 26-ring Sholl curve with peak 73 at r/R_max = 0.6176, 62 bifurcation hubs, D_f = 1.7817 +- 0.0248) and the 6-panel comparison figure aligns the bf = 0.20 and bf = 0.70 model arbors with the specimen. Pass 3 adds the 4-panel coincidence figure whose Panel A renders the electrotonic tree with tip pairs and LCA hotspots. Deductions, larger than in v2 because the Pass 3 audit looked at where the specimen numbers come from: the specimen reference values the figure and measurements are \"matched\" against (`specimen_metadata.sholl_peak_intersections_ref` = 73, `skeleton_branch_points_ref` = 62, `box_counting_fractal_dimension_ref` = 1.7817; reference JSON L98-102) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs written back into the dataset, so value == reference by construction and the self-test (L1388-1389) merely pins a regression (-5); the new Ca2+ hotspot layer is compared with no specimen at all — no Llinás & Sugimori (1980) dendritic spike trace, no Polsky (2004) summation curve — so the coincidence figure is model-only (-3); the model-arbor-vs-specimen comparison still rests on Sholl shape and D_f alone, with no branch-angle or segment-length histogram against the drawing (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L1386–L1390: Self-test suite 7 hard-codes sholl_peak_count == 73 and n_branch_points == 62 (regression pin, not an empirical check) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L1386-L1390>",
        "datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json L88–L102: specimen_metadata *_ref values (73, 420.0, 0.6176, 62, 1.7817) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs recorded as references — match by construction, not an independent morphometric <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/cajal_dendritic_wiring_reference.json#L88-L102>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-specimen-match-2>,
