<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2007, 2010) Greedy MST Wiring-vs-Conduction-Delay Cost Trade-Off Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves Ramón y Cajal's (1899) trade-off between minimum wiring length at bf = 0 (Prim/Steiner MST) and minimum soma-to-synapse path length at bf = 1 (radial star graph), with exact critical transition threshold bf_c = (d_rv - d_uv) / d_ru | Variables: d_uv = ||u - v||: Euclidean distance from tree node u to carrier target v; d_ru = path(u, root): path length along tree from soma root to u; bf in [0, 1]: Cuntz balancing factor weighting conduction time vs cytoplasmic cable length" ;
    dct:source "Cuntz, Forstner, Borst & Häusser (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. 6(8):e1000877 Results & Fig. 1; Cuntz, Borst & Segev (2007) PNAS 104:13319-13324" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L165-L207>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_058_cajal_dendritic_wiring.lean#L36-L67> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled (S bf_s d_uv path_u : Int) : Int :=
  S * d_uv + bf_s * path_u
theorem cuntz_2010_wiring_delay_cost_tradeoff
    (S d_ru d_uv d_rv bf_s : Int)
    (hS : 0 < S) (h_wire : d_uv < d_rv) (h_tri : d_rv < d_ru + d_uv) :
    cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled S bf_s d_uv d_ru -
      cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled S bf_s d_rv 0 =
      bf_s * d_ru - S * (d_rv - d_uv) ∧
    0 < cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled S 0 d_rv 0 -
      cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled S 0 d_uv d_ru ∧
    0 < cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled S S d_uv d_ru -
      cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled S S d_rv 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "C(u, v) = ||u - v|| + bf * path(u, root);  C_S(u, v) - C_S(root, v) = bf_s * d_ru - S * (d_rv - d_uv)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0014-4886(59)90046-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(81)84782-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nn1253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704731104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7793.2001.00445.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.1980.sp013358>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00280.2007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000877>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.48637> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Ramón y Cajal Minimum-Wiring-Length & Conduction-Delay Greedy Steiner Dendritic Trees + Rall's 3/2 Power Law" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.cuntz_greedy_cost_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.cuntz_2010_wiring_delay_cost_tradeoff" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Rall's (1959) 3/2 Electrotonic Impedance-Matching Diameter Power Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that Rall's 3/2 power law matches input conductance across dendritic bifurcations so the branched arbor collapses to an equivalent electrotonic cylinder, with symmetric parent diameter d_p = 2^(2/3) d strictly steeper than Murray's vascular cube law (d_p = 2^(1/3) d) | Variables: d_parent, d_1, d_2: parent and daughter dendritic cylinder diameters; g_k = d_k^(3/2): electrotonic input conductance scaling variable" ;
    dct:source "Rall (1959) Exp. Neurol. 1(5):491-527 Eqs. 9-16; Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. 6(8):e1000877 Fig. 2" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L208-L237>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_058_cajal_dendritic_wiring.lean#L85-L115> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def rall_cubed_diameter (g : Int) : Int := g * g
def rall_parent_half_cube (g1 g2 : Int) : Int := g1 + g2
theorem rall_1959_three_halves_impedance_matching
    (g1 g2 g : Int) (hg : 0 < g) :
    rall_cubed_diameter (rall_parent_half_cube g1 g2) =
      rall_cubed_diameter g1 + rall_cubed_diameter g2 + 2 * g1 * g2 ∧
    rall_cubed_diameter (rall_parent_half_cube g g) =
      4 * rall_cubed_diameter g ∧
    2 * rall_cubed_diameter g <
      rall_cubed_diameter (rall_parent_half_cube g g)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d_parent^(3/2) = d_1^(3/2) + d_2^(3/2)  =>  d_parent^3 = d_1^3 + d_2^3 + 2 (d_1 d_2)^(3/2);  symmetric (d_1 = d_2 = d): d_parent^3 = 4 d^3 (d_parent = 2^(2/3) d)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0014-4886(59)90046-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(81)84782-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nn1253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704731104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7793.2001.00445.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.1980.sp013358>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00280.2007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000877>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.48637> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Ramón y Cajal Minimum-Wiring-Length & Conduction-Delay Greedy Steiner Dendritic Trees + Rall's 3/2 Power Law" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.rall_cubed_diameter" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.rall_1959_three_halves_impedance_matching" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Acyclic Dendritic Spanning Tree & Binary Bifurcation Topological Identity" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees zero cycle formation (beta_1 = 0, unique soma-to-synapse electrotonic path) and exact conservation of leaves vs bifurcations (L = B + 1) in binary dendritic arbors | Variables: B: internal dendritic bifurcation points; L: terminal synaptic carrier tips; N: total nodes including soma root; E: total dendritic cable segments; beta_1: first Betti cycle number" ;
    dct:source "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. 6(8):e1000877 Methods" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L238-L280>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_058_cajal_dendritic_wiring.lean#L127-L149> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def binary_arbor_leaves (B : Int) : Int := B + 1
def binary_arbor_nodes (B : Int) : Int := 1 + B + binary_arbor_leaves B
def binary_arbor_edges (B : Int) : Int := 2 * B + 1
def tree_betti_1 (N E : Int) : Int := E - N + 1
theorem dendritic_binary_tree_topology_identity (B : Int) :
    binary_arbor_edges B = binary_arbor_nodes B - 1 ∧
    binary_arbor_leaves B - binary_arbor_edges B + B = 0 ∧
    tree_betti_1 (binary_arbor_nodes B) (binary_arbor_edges B) = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "E = N - 1,  L = B + 1,  E = 2B + 1,  beta_1 = E - N + 1 = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0014-4886(59)90046-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(81)84782-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nn1253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704731104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7793.2001.00445.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.1980.sp013358>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00280.2007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000877>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.48637> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Ramón y Cajal Minimum-Wiring-Length & Conduction-Delay Greedy Steiner Dendritic Trees + Rall's 3/2 Power Law" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.binary_arbor_edges" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.dendritic_binary_tree_topology_identity" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Rall (1959) Passive Membrane Exact Linear Superposition (Coincidence-Detection Null Model)" ;
    dct:description "Establishes the exact linear null model (superposition ratio 1, identical-input gain 2) for the passive Rall cable ablation (g_Ca = 0, K+ gate frozen) of the Morris-Lecar Ca2+ hotspot; the measured active supralinear gain (> 2) and coincidence window are deviations from this theorem, so coincidence detection is attributable to the regenerative g_Ca term alone | Variables: V_k: hotspot membrane potential from rest at forward-Euler step k; I_k: attenuated alpha-function synaptic current; a = 1 - dt (g_L + g_K w_rest)/C, b = dt/C: discrete passive RC coefficients (scaled integers); I_a, I_b: the two tip-pair synaptic current trains" ;
    dct:source "Rall (1959) Exp. Neurol. 1(5):491-527 (passive cable linearity); Morris & Lecar (1981) Biophys. J. 35:193-213 (active hotspot); Polsky, Mel & Schiller (2004) Nat. Neurosci. 7:621-627 (within-branch supralinear vs between-branch linear summation)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L425-L463>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_058_cajal_dendritic_wiring.lean#L163-L182> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def lin_rc_step (a b V I : Int) : Int := a * V + b * I
def lin_rc_traj (a b : Int) (I : Nat → Int) : Nat → Int
  | 0 => 0
  | k + 1 => lin_rc_step a b (lin_rc_traj a b I k) (I k)
theorem rall_passive_membrane_linear_superposition
    (a b : Int) (Ia Ib : Nat → Int) (k : Nat) :
    lin_rc_traj a b (fun n => Ia n + Ib n) k =
      lin_rc_traj a b Ia k + lin_rc_traj a b Ib k ∧
    lin_rc_traj a b (fun n => 2 * Ia n) k = 2 * lin_rc_traj a b Ia k
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "V_{k+1} = a V_k + b I_k, V_0 = 0  =>  V[I_a + I_b](k) = V[I_a](k) + V[I_b](k)  and  V[2 I](k) = 2 V[I](k)  (passive paired/single peak gain = 2 exactly)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0014-4886(59)90046-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(81)84782-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nn1253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704731104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7793.2001.00445.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.1980.sp013358>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00280.2007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000877>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.48637> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Ramón y Cajal Minimum-Wiring-Length & Conduction-Delay Greedy Steiner Dendritic Trees + Rall's 3/2 Power Law" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.lin_rc_traj" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.rall_passive_membrane_linear_superposition" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Koch (1999) / Rall (1959) Sinusoidal Steady-State Length-Constant Bound" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees that the electrotonic distances X_e = l_e / lambda_f(d_e) accumulated along the Cuntz tree (tip -> LCA hotspot -> soma) are never shorter than their DC values, so passive synaptic attenuation exp(-X) at the alpha-synapse frequency is at least as strong as at DC and the AC/DC ratio lambda_f/lambda_DC = 0.2487 reported by the script is bounded by 1 | Variables: lambda_DC: Rall DC length constant of a cylinder of diameter d (R_m membrane resistivity, R_i axial resistivity); lambda_f: sinusoidal steady-state length constant at synaptic frequency f; tau_m = R_m C_m; s = sqrt(1 + (omega tau_m)^2); lf2 = lambda_f^2, ld2 = lambda_DC^2 (scaled integers); X_e: electrotonic edge length of Rall-3/2 segment e" ;
    dct:source "Rall (1959) Exp. Neurol. 1(5):491-527 Eq. 2; Koch (1999) Biophysics of Computation, Oxford Univ. Press, Ch. 2 Eq. 2.37; Roth & Häusser (2001) J. Physiol. 535(2):445-472 Table 2 (Purkinje R_m, R_i, C_m)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L352-L390>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_058_cajal_dendritic_wiring.lean#L197-L214> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def koch_ac_length_relation (s lf2 ld2 : Int) : Prop := (1 + s) * lf2 = 2 * ld2
theorem koch_ac_length_constant_bound
    (s lf2 ld2 : Int) (hs : 1 ≤ s) (hlf : 0 ≤ lf2)
    (hrel : koch_ac_length_relation s lf2 ld2) :
    lf2 ≤ ld2 ∧ (s = 1 → lf2 = ld2)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "lambda_DC(d) = sqrt(R_m d / (4 R_i));  lambda_f = lambda_DC sqrt(2 / (1 + s)), s = sqrt(1 + (2 pi f tau_m)^2) >= 1;  (1 + s) lambda_f^2 = 2 lambda_DC^2  =>  lambda_f^2 <= lambda_DC^2 (equality iff s = 1);  X_e = l_e / lambda_f(d_e)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0014-4886(59)90046-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(81)84782-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nn1253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704731104>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-7793.2001.00445.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1113/jphysiol.1980.sp013358>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1152/jn.00280.2007>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1000877>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.48637> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Ramón y Cajal Minimum-Wiring-Length & Conduction-Delay Greedy Steiner Dendritic Trees + Rall's 3/2 Power Law" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.koch_ac_length_relation" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_058.koch_ac_length_constant_bound" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

